    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1824">

                <pb facs="1334" n="1218" sameAs="frus:frus1915/pg1218"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 319.1123L25/20.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Minister Price.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 192.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-10-19">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 19, 1915</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The Department has received your No. 630,
                    of the 1st instant, with which you enclose copies of statements of claims for
                    damages against the Republic of Panama for injuries suffered by American
                    soldiers in the Colon riot of April 2, 1915 (with the exception of the case of
                    Corporal Maurice Langdon, who was killed), which statements were sent to your
                    Legation by Brigadier General C. R. Edwards, Military Commander of the Canal
                    Zone.</p>
                <p>In reply you are informed that the Department will, in due time, give the
                    statements careful consideration.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State: <lb/>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Frank L. Polk.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
